# Copy to `.env` and fill in with your own Firebase project's values (from
# the Firebase console: Project settings > General > Your apps > SDK setup
# and configuration) once cross-device sync is ready to go live. See
# docs/adr/0006 for what these are for and why they're safe to be public
# (they identify the project, they don't grant access - Firestore Security
# Rules do that).
#
# Leave this file (and a missing/absent .env) alone for local development -
# src/cloudSync.ts defaults to the "demo-times-tables-quizzer" project,
# which only ever talks to the local Firebase emulator (npm run test:rules,
# or `firebase emulators:start`), never a real cloud project.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
